{
  "description": "Round 6 of the full-parity phase (sandbox family, the tree with the P43 fix). The sandbox family puts no NAN into its data (crates/twig-fuzz/src/generators/sandbox.rs), so its 30000 generated cases (seeds 17001-17015, no mismatch) cannot show the array walk P43 fixed: these hand-written probes check it in the family's settings. SecurityChecker::doEnsureToStringAllowed() hands an array to ensureToStringAllowedForArray() before its isSandboxed() check, and ensureSpreadAllowed() walks its materialised operand whether sandboxed or not (TWIG/src/Sandbox/SecurityChecker.php:154-243); the walk evaluates `!$v` for every element, where PHP 8.5 warns `unexpected NAN value was coerced to bool` (i_zend_is_true(), PHPSRC/Zend/zend_operators.h). Covered: a global policy, `{% sandbox %}`, `include(..., sandboxed = true)` and a source policy (`\"sandbox\": {\"source_policy\": [...]}`), on both sides of the sandbox, the order of the warning and a SecurityNotAllowedMethodError, spreads, Traversables (an Iterator walked only when sandboxed, an IteratorAggregate's elements handed on without `!$v`), template name lists, `{% deprecated %}`, `_context`, arrow function results, dynamic mapping keys, falsy SimpleXMLElements, `\"errors\": \"throw\"`. Every vector matches the oracle and must keep replaying identically. Recorded with \"isolation\": \"process\".",
